# Worktree agent context (${SLUG})

This checkout is an isolated git worktree. Prefer tooling commands that target it explicitly.

## Identity

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Slug | `${SLUG}` |
| Branch | `${BRANCH}` |
| Compose project | `${COMPOSE_PROJECT}` |
| Site origin | `${SITE_ORIGIN}` |
| Base env | `${BASE_ENV}` |
| Worktree path | `${WORKTREE_PATH}` |
| Parent repo | `${PARENT_REPO}` |
| Media path | `${MEDIA_PATH}` |

## Commands

From the **parent** checkout (recommended — no `cd` / direnv):

```bash
uv run dk --worktree ${SLUG} …
uv run dk worktree up ${SLUG}
uv run dk worktree down ${SLUG}
uv run dk worktree context ${SLUG} --json
```

Inside this worktree, `dk ${BASE_ENV}` uses the remapped compose project and localdev hostnames.

## Rules

- Read the repo `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/` (especially secrets and remote environments).
- **Do not** run remote deploy envs (`staging`, `prod`, or any env with `docker_host`) from this worktree unless the user explicitly confirms target and action.
- Never decrypt or print SOPS credentials in agent sessions.

See `docs/WORKTREES.md` in catalpa-workspace-tooling.
